>My order of preference, from worst to best is:

>la DJENifer
>la DJEnifer
>la djEnifer
>la djénifer
>la djenifer

>i.e., I prefer that the name be fully adapted, but if they insist
>on the unusual stress then mark it with the least intrusive method.

This is my preference also.

In handwriting (where I also use cyrillic letters as often as not, without
really thinking about it) I almost always put an acute or a macron over the
vowel rather than capitalizing anything. This is technically worng, I
believe, but I'm not doing any formal writing in Lojban so I don't care.

